<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.2.2: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00389</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.2.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ffbb09bb-e4b1-4415-a350-c00a0ab9267a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>A streaming service offers two options for subscription plans. Option A charges $10.99 a month plus $2 per movie. Option B charges $5.99 a month plus $3 per movie. The table below describes this. Which of the following systems of equations represents the two options for one month?</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>\(x\) (Number of movies</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>0</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>1</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>2</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>3</emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Option A</emphasis></entry><entry>10.99</entry>
      <entry>12.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
      <entry>16.99</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Option B</emphasis></entry><entry>5.99</entry>
      <entry>8.99</entry>
      <entry>11.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>
</content>
</document>
